WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:05.502
Mr. Freaky ran over. "What's going on?"

2
00:00:05.503 --> 00:00:10.192
"Mayor Hubbletree wants to cut Oswald open!" Waldo cried.

3
00:00:10.193 --> 00:00:12.878
Winnie looked at Mrs. Hubbletree.

4
00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:16.397
"Do you have any proof that Oswald ate Bowie?"

5
00:00:16.398 --> 00:00:21.642
"Yes!" Mayor Hubbletree said. "He grabbed your kitten!"

6
00:00:21.643 --> 00:00:25.333
"But he didn't eat Inky," Waldo said.

7
00:00:25.334 --> 00:00:29.120
"He just took her for a ride!" Sid added.

8
00:00:29.121 --> 00:00:32.253
"Do something, Freaky!" the mayor snapped.

9
00:00:32.254 --> 00:00:35.646
"Before I knock down your school!"

10
00:00:35.647 --> 00:00:40.821
"Oh . . ." Mr. Freaky reached for his handkerchief.

11
00:00:40.822 --> 00:00:43.794
Miss Bungle came over to Mayor Hubbletree.

12
00:00:43.795 --> 00:00:50.343
"The search is still going on. No need to panic yet."

13
00:00:50.344 --> 00:00:53.652
"Maybe Bowie found his way back home," Sid said.

14
00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:56.289
"Maybe he's in his terrarium."

15
00:00:56.290 --> 00:00:58.755
Mrs. Hubbletree sniffed.

16
00:00:58.756 --> 00:01:02.229
"He does like to hide under his bridge when he's scared."

17
00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:05.915
Sid ran toward the gecko's terrarium.

18
00:01:05.916 --> 00:01:07.873
"Nope. He's not here."

19
00:01:07.874 --> 00:01:11.494
"You barely looked for him," Mrs. Hubbletree said.

20
00:01:11.495 --> 00:01:14.033
"How can you be sure?"

21
00:01:14.034 --> 00:01:17.087
"Sid's allergic to geckos," Ben explained.

22
00:01:17.088 --> 00:01:22.024
"If Bowie were in there, Sid would be covered with green spots."

23
00:01:22.025 --> 00:01:26.429
"Where else does Bowie like to hide?" Sid asked.

24
00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:29.610
"Under the couch," Mrs. Hubbletree said.

25
00:01:29.611 --> 00:01:33.936
"And . . ." Her words trailed off as she stared at Sid.

26
00:01:33.937 --> 00:01:39.361
Ben gulped. Fresh new spots covered Sid.

27
00:01:39.362 --> 00:01:43.683
"That's weird," Ben thought. "No animals are nearby."

28
00:01:43.684 --> 00:01:46.418
Could Sid be allergic to people too?

29
00:01:46.419 --> 00:01:50.915
Suddenly his eyes flicked back to Mrs. Hubbletree.

30
00:01:50.916 --> 00:01:53.393
"Nobody move!" Ben whispered.

31
00:01:53.394 --> 00:01:57.443
He lifted a finger and pointed at Mrs. Hubbletree's handbag.

32
00:01:57.444 --> 00:01:58.981
"I found him!"

33
00:01:58.982 --> 00:02:02.983
"Bowie!" Mrs. Hubbletree cried.

34
00:02:02.984 --> 00:02:08.620
The gecko was clinging to her handbag—perfectly blending in with the bag's colors.

35
00:02:08.621 --> 00:02:13.062
Waldo grinned. "I told you Oswald was innocent!"

36
00:02:13.063 --> 00:02:20.641
The room filled with cheers as everyone learned that Bowie had been found.

37
00:02:20.642 --> 00:02:26.506
"Now we can have the best pet contest!" someone shouted.

38
00:02:26.507 --> 00:02:32.046
Miss Bungle nodded. "Contestants, line up again with your pets.

39
00:02:32.047 --> 00:02:38.074
During the show our pet adoption volunteers will bring around some of the available animals.

40
00:02:38.075 --> 00:02:41.907
Please consider taking one home."

41
00:02:41.908 --> 00:02:43.684
Ben glanced at Sid.

42
00:02:43.685 --> 00:02:47.447
His little brother's eyes were filled with tears.

43
00:02:47.448 --> 00:02:49.974
"It's okay, Sid," Ben said.

44
00:02:49.975 --> 00:02:52.769
"Maybe we can come back next year and find a pet."

45
00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:55.338
Sid just hung his head.

46
00:02:55.339 --> 00:03:01.008
"The show's starting," Winnie called. "Come on over and sit with us."

47
00:03:01.009 --> 00:03:04.966
Ben watched the stage, waiting for Rex-Rex's turn.

48
00:03:04.967 --> 00:03:11.804
At last, the two-headed dog trotted proudly across the stage, keeping his eyes on Mog.

49
00:03:11.805 --> 00:03:19.287
Winnie reached out to pet the skeleton dog that was passing by with Samantha. "He's cute!"

50
00:03:19.288 --> 00:03:21.545
"I like him too," Sid said.

51
00:03:21.546 --> 00:03:23.383
"We met him before at the booth.

52
00:03:23.384 --> 00:03:28.461
He gave me spots, but I didn't care." He petted the dog too.

53
00:03:28.462 --> 00:03:30.869
"Be careful, Sid," Ben warned.

54
00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:32.989
"Mom and Dad are picking us up soon.

55
00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:38.080
If you're still covered in spots . . ." His words trailed off as something clicked.

56
00:03:38.081 --> 00:03:41.211
"Actually, keep petting that dog!"

57
00:03:41.212 --> 00:03:47.171
"Huh?" Sid said. The skeleton dog wagged its tail and gave him a kiss.

58
00:03:47.172 --> 00:03:50.648
"Why are you telling me to keep petting him, Ben?"

59
00:03:50.649 --> 00:03:55.225
"Because I don't see any new spots!"

60
00:03:55.226 --> 00:04:00.738
Sid looked down. "Me neither!"

61
00:04:00.739 --> 00:04:06.087
Samantha smiled. "Bones is available for adoption, if you'd like to take him home."

62
00:04:06.088 --> 00:04:09.288
Sid had solved the mystery too.

63
00:04:09.289 --> 00:04:13.765
"When I was petting Bones earlier, I was holding a ferret.

64
00:04:13.766 --> 00:04:20.516
So maybe I'm not allergic to Bones—I'm allergic to the ferret! Oh wow." Sid grinned.

65
00:04:20.517 --> 00:04:23.585
"Ben, can we adopt him?"

66
00:04:23.586 --> 00:04:26.272
"I don't know," Ben said doubtfully.

67
00:04:26.273 --> 00:04:29.161
"You know how Mom feels about dogs."

68
00:04:29.162 --> 00:04:32.349
"Bones is so cute! Maybe she'll like him."

69
00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:34.501
"We'll find out when she shows up soon.

70
00:04:34.502 --> 00:04:37.547
But don't get your hopes up," Ben warned.

71
00:04:37.548 --> 00:04:41.737
Onstage, the contest was nearly over.

72
00:04:41.738 --> 00:04:45.180
First, the judges awarded third prize.

73
00:04:45.181 --> 00:04:49.338
It went to a vampire cat that did flips.

74
00:04:49.339 --> 00:04:51.873
Miss Bungle made the next announcement.

75
00:04:51.874 --> 00:04:56.378
"Second prize goes to . . . Rex-Rex!"

76
00:04:56.379 --> 00:04:58.434
"Yes!" Ben shouted.

77
00:04:58.435 --> 00:05:03.795
Before the judges announced the final prize, Ben's phone rang.

78
00:05:03.796 --> 00:05:09.135
It was his mom. "We have to go, Sid."

79
00:05:09.136 --> 00:05:18.781
When Ben and Sid went to meet their parents, Bones trotted behind them.

80
00:05:18.782 --> 00:05:20.895
Ben's mother frowned.

81
00:05:20.896 --> 00:05:26.068
"This is Bones!" Sid called.

82
00:05:26.069 --> 00:05:28.200
"Can we adopt him, Mom? Please?"

83
00:05:28.201 --> 00:05:30.513
"I said, no—"

84
00:05:30.514 --> 00:05:34.523
"Woof!" With a loud bark, Bones bounded toward their mother.

85
00:05:34.524 --> 00:05:37.842
He took a flying leap into her arms.

86
00:05:37.843 --> 00:05:43.293
Everyone laughed, including Ben's mother.

87
00:05:43.294 --> 00:05:47.858
"See!" Sid cried. "He's a great dog!"

88
00:05:47.859 --> 00:05:51.960
"Hold out your arms, Sid," their mother said, putting the dog down.

89
00:05:51.961 --> 00:05:55.467
Sid obeyed. "No spots!"

90
00:05:55.468 --> 00:06:00.600
"So . . .?" Ben held his breath and looked at his mother.

91
00:06:00.601 --> 00:06:05.624
"Can we keep him?" Sid asked. "Please?"

92
00:06:05.625 --> 00:06:12.139
Slowly their mother nodded, and Ben could feel a grin spreading from ear to ear.

93
00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:15.352
He dropped down to give Bones a hug.

94
00:06:15.353 --> 00:06:18.293
"Want to go back in the gym?" Sid asked.

95
00:06:18.294 --> 00:06:22.390
"We can find out which pet won first prize in the best pet contest."

96
00:06:22.391 --> 00:06:35.452
"Nope," Ben said. The best pet was right here, licking his face!

